WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.315
- Worth it Japan.

00:00:01.315 --> 00:00:03.026
Adam, Andrew, and I are taking on Tokyo.

00:00:03.026 --> 00:00:04.908
This is part two of a
three part Japan series.

00:00:04.908 --> 00:00:06.331
Today we're doing coffee.

00:00:06.331 --> 00:00:08.663
We brought our good
friend, Tasty producer,

00:00:08.663 --> 00:00:11.791
bodyguard, translator, Rie McClenny.

00:00:11.791 --> 00:00:12.624
- Hi.

00:00:12.624 --> 00:00:14.313
- It's really hot here.
(laughs)

00:00:14.313 --> 00:00:17.813
- And sweaty boy himself, Andrew Ilnyckyj.

00:00:20.068 --> 00:00:21.405
I don't know why I opened my mouth.

00:00:21.405 --> 00:00:23.292
Today on Worth it Japan,
we're going to be trying

00:00:23.292 --> 00:00:25.258
three coffees at three
drastically different price points

00:00:25.258 --> 00:00:27.708
to find out which coffee is
the most worth it at its price.

00:00:27.708 --> 00:00:28.541
- Worth it.

00:00:28.541 --> 00:00:31.608
- There's a very special
coffee that we found,

00:00:31.608 --> 00:00:34.037
that kind of, in some
ways, motivated this trip,

00:00:34.037 --> 00:00:35.303
that we're going to get
to a little bit later,

00:00:35.303 --> 00:00:36.261
and here we go.

00:00:36.261 --> 00:00:38.844
(upbeat music)

00:01:02.598 --> 00:01:04.346
- Why is it important that, as a company,

00:01:04.346 --> 00:01:07.013
you are roasting your own beans?

00:01:52.990 --> 00:01:56.448
- So what we're having is... there it is.

00:01:56.448 --> 00:01:57.859
That and that.

00:01:57.859 --> 00:01:59.833
- How do you say cheers in Japanese?

00:01:59.833 --> 00:02:00.666
- 'Kanpai'

00:02:05.888 --> 00:02:08.242
- Wow
- That is powerful.

00:02:08.242 --> 00:02:11.161
- Super strong.
- Yeah, tastes like ambition.

00:02:11.161 --> 00:02:13.553
- Bitterness and a
little bit of sweetness.

00:02:13.553 --> 00:02:15.553
- Do you usually go for iced coffee?

00:02:15.553 --> 00:02:18.249
- Always. I take my beverages very slowly.

00:02:18.249 --> 00:02:20.089
Iced coffee, you can
enjoy for a much longer

00:02:20.089 --> 00:02:21.790
period of time than a hot cup of coffee.

00:02:21.790 --> 00:02:25.110
- You also have the dangerous
game with this where you..

00:02:25.110 --> 00:02:29.464
- Oh I'm very familiar
with missing the straw.

00:02:29.464 --> 00:02:31.466
I don't know if everybody
does it that way.

00:02:31.466 --> 00:02:33.064
I also love how there's
a bunch of people here,

00:02:33.064 --> 00:02:34.963
just doing their own work: studying,

00:02:34.963 --> 00:02:36.883
starting their own company--
- Dreamers.

00:02:36.883 --> 00:02:38.172
You don't know where you're going,

00:02:38.172 --> 00:02:42.167
but it all starts with a good cup of...

00:02:42.167 --> 00:02:43.836
- R.O.
(laughs)

00:02:43.836 --> 00:02:47.169
Jetlag solved, at least for a few hours.

00:02:48.929 --> 00:02:50.142
R.O.Star.

00:02:50.142 --> 00:02:52.228
- R.O.Star.
- R.O.Star.

00:02:52.228 --> 00:02:53.395
- Coffee fact.

00:02:54.783 --> 00:02:55.616
- What's up, Adam?

00:02:55.616 --> 00:02:57.108
The first coffee shop in Tokyo.

00:02:57.108 --> 00:02:58.947
Guess what year it was founded?

00:02:58.947 --> 00:02:59.780
- 1887.

00:03:01.311 --> 00:03:03.004
- Wait, you did not see my fact did you?

00:03:03.004 --> 00:03:05.031
- No, but I made an educated guess.

00:03:05.031 --> 00:03:07.401
- That was amazing.

00:03:07.401 --> 00:03:09.484
- What year is it?
- 1888.

00:03:10.631 --> 00:03:12.026
So we're going to Coffee
Elementary School.

00:03:12.026 --> 00:03:13.443
Rie, can you give us some background?

00:03:13.443 --> 00:03:15.213
- The barista used to be a teacher.

00:03:15.213 --> 00:03:16.815
- What kind of teacher?

00:03:16.815 --> 00:03:19.217
- Elementary school teacher.
- Oh.

00:03:19.217 --> 00:03:20.248
(laughs)

00:03:20.248 --> 00:03:22.831
(upbeat music)

00:03:36.054 --> 00:03:39.554
So is your coffee for elementary students?

00:04:51.131 --> 00:04:53.029
- It really does smell like chocolate.

00:04:53.029 --> 00:04:55.612
- Floral chocolate, it's like
a chocolate of rose petals.

00:04:55.612 --> 00:04:59.332
- I love the handmade mug. I
mean, the way they make this

00:04:59.332 --> 00:05:02.381
is by going like this on
clay, right? But it does also

00:05:02.381 --> 00:05:04.516
mold to the hand very...
- Is this clay?

00:05:04.516 --> 00:05:06.339
- It could be. Cheers.

00:05:06.339 --> 00:05:07.839
- Kanpai.
- Kanpai.

00:05:11.267 --> 00:05:13.927
- If this were a color,
this is like pastel beige.

00:05:13.927 --> 00:05:15.745
- Warm in hugging but not aggressive.

00:05:15.745 --> 00:05:18.474
- It's crazy how smooth this coffee is.

00:05:18.474 --> 00:05:23.146
- It's almost like a coffee
tea. Do you taste blueberries?

00:05:23.146 --> 00:05:24.119
- A little bit.

00:05:24.119 --> 00:05:25.921
- This is like an episode of Scooby Doo.

00:05:25.921 --> 00:05:28.427
There is this blueberry
that pulls off a rubber mask

00:05:28.427 --> 00:05:29.747
and it's like, oh my god.

00:05:29.747 --> 00:05:31.744
That coffee was a
blueberry this whole time,

00:05:31.744 --> 00:05:35.077
and it just blew your mind into berries.

00:05:36.496 --> 00:05:38.611
- I am starting to get the coffee jitters.

00:05:38.611 --> 00:05:42.117
You know what this coffee
really boils down to?

00:05:42.117 --> 00:05:43.933
Ha ha ha, boils.
- Boil.

00:05:43.933 --> 00:05:45.926
I don't think it technically boils but--

00:05:45.926 --> 00:05:47.975
- You know you put boiling
water over coffee beans?

00:05:47.975 --> 00:05:50.447
- It's actually below boiling.
- Just below boiling.

00:05:50.447 --> 00:05:51.678
- Anyway, what were you gonna say?

00:05:51.678 --> 00:05:54.615
- I don't even remember. Wow
this coffee is hitting me.

00:05:54.615 --> 00:05:57.115
This is great. Let's go party.

00:05:59.157 --> 00:06:02.634
- Oh, blueberry. It's like
how did you get in here?

00:06:02.634 --> 00:06:04.717
(laughs)

00:06:08.252 --> 00:06:09.747
- We had the first two locations in Tokyo,

00:06:09.747 --> 00:06:13.299
and now to find the most
expensive coffee in Osaka.

00:06:13.299 --> 00:06:15.280
Rie told us to pick
these up before we left.

00:06:15.280 --> 00:06:18.934
- This is bento box.
- Oh lunch box.

00:06:18.934 --> 00:06:23.101
Rie always picks the best
stuff, as you would expect.

00:06:24.927 --> 00:06:29.852
- This is my dessert, I
shouldn't have eaten it first.

00:06:29.852 --> 00:06:32.154
- Did you know that in
the Kanagawa Prefecture,

00:06:32.154 --> 00:06:34.503
there's a unison hot spring theme park

00:06:34.503 --> 00:06:38.586
and there you can take
baths in real warm coffee.

00:06:39.817 --> 00:06:41.675
- Why do they do it?
- Refresh yourself,

00:06:41.675 --> 00:06:43.439
and also it's good for
your skin apparently.

00:06:43.439 --> 00:06:45.335
- So instead of drinking
coffee in the morning,

00:06:45.335 --> 00:06:48.272
I could just steep myself
in a bath of coffee.

00:06:48.272 --> 00:06:49.939
- Yeah, pretty much.

00:06:54.053 --> 00:06:56.970
(orchestral music)

00:07:11.342 --> 00:07:14.009
- Why did you barrel-age coffee?

00:08:11.550 --> 00:08:12.773
- What is so important about making it

00:08:12.773 --> 00:08:14.856
and doing it that slowly?

00:08:38.368 --> 00:08:42.970
- We have a 100,000 yen cup of
coffee right in front of us.

00:08:42.970 --> 00:08:45.361
I have a lot of emotions. I feel weird.

00:08:45.361 --> 00:08:47.669
What if I die? I also am excited though.

00:08:47.669 --> 00:08:49.696
- Really we started a coffee episode

00:08:49.696 --> 00:08:53.423
and we're ending up
somewhere in a wine episode.

00:08:53.423 --> 00:08:56.083
This is aged, something you sip,

00:08:56.083 --> 00:08:58.300
we're here at night,
we're no longer doing this

00:08:58.300 --> 00:09:00.367
the way that coffee is normally consumed.

00:09:00.367 --> 00:09:03.838
- Yeah, we went from coffee to cof o'wine.

00:09:03.838 --> 00:09:05.737
- Cof o'wine, it's a new pokemon.

00:09:05.737 --> 00:09:06.822
- Cof o'wine.

00:09:06.822 --> 00:09:08.066
- So we have to take turns obviously,

00:09:08.066 --> 00:09:09.772
we can't drink out the
cup at the same time.

00:09:09.772 --> 00:09:13.917
Is there a Japanese translation
of rock, paper, scissors?

00:09:13.917 --> 00:09:15.417
- Jan-ken-pon
- Aww

00:09:17.115 --> 00:09:20.513
- First, we smell. (sniffs)

00:09:20.513 --> 00:09:24.209
Holy schmoly, it really
does smell like wine.

00:09:24.209 --> 00:09:25.917
- I'm getting chocolate from it too.

00:09:25.917 --> 00:09:28.802
- This is the darkest
liquid I've ever seen.

00:09:28.802 --> 00:09:31.078
- Should we drink?
- Okay yeah, we should drink.

00:09:31.078 --> 00:09:34.995
I'm really nervous. I'm
super nervous actually.

00:09:36.242 --> 00:09:39.159
(orchestral music)

00:09:44.265 --> 00:09:46.604
Wow. I've never tasted
anything like this before.

00:09:46.604 --> 00:09:47.672
- Is it actually good?

00:09:47.672 --> 00:09:50.481
- Oh yeah, it's very good.
Ooh, I want a second sip.

00:09:50.481 --> 00:09:51.626
But I'll let you have a sip first.

00:09:51.626 --> 00:09:53.012
- You really amped this up for me.

00:09:53.012 --> 00:09:54.257
I'm scared to lift it too high

00:09:54.257 --> 00:09:56.904
because it's gonna look awkward.

00:09:56.904 --> 00:09:59.821
(orchestral music)

00:10:02.047 --> 00:10:04.382
- Whoa. It's really good.

00:10:04.382 --> 00:10:07.065
It's like somebody took a chocolate taser

00:10:07.065 --> 00:10:09.601
and just rammed it into my mouth.

00:10:09.601 --> 00:10:13.108
- This tastes a lot like a dessert wine.

00:10:13.108 --> 00:10:15.944
Instead of making chocolate
milk, it's like you used wine

00:10:15.944 --> 00:10:18.603
instead of milk and you
made chocolate wine.

00:10:18.603 --> 00:10:20.677
Should I be worried
that this is fermented,

00:10:20.677 --> 00:10:23.527
that this is alcoholic? Is
this gonna make me drunk?

00:10:23.527 --> 00:10:25.571
Is it okay to drink a whole cup of this?

00:10:25.571 --> 00:10:26.923
Are you sure that this is not alcoholic?

00:10:26.923 --> 00:10:28.443
'Cause I feel pretty weird right now.

00:10:28.443 --> 00:10:31.840
- Here's what I know. This
is absolutely worth trying.

00:10:31.840 --> 00:10:33.878
- It's pretty yummy, I'm not gonna lie.

00:10:33.878 --> 00:10:36.878
- Come on over, Adam and Rie.
- Okay.

00:10:46.468 --> 00:10:50.053
- What's so funny?
(laughs)

00:10:50.053 --> 00:10:51.734
- Coffee. Coffee.

00:10:51.734 --> 00:10:53.153
- Steven's had a lot of coffee.

00:10:53.153 --> 00:10:54.570
- Coffee. Coffee.

00:10:55.550 --> 00:10:56.723
Which coffee was the most worth it

00:10:56.723 --> 00:10:57.640
and surprise for you guys?

00:10:57.640 --> 00:10:59.354
- This one is actually really hard.

00:10:59.354 --> 00:11:01.739
There was my favorite one,
Coffee Elementary School.

00:11:01.739 --> 00:11:04.924
The guy was so cool, great
location, and possibly the best

00:11:04.924 --> 00:11:07.037
tasting cup of coffee I've ever had.

00:11:07.037 --> 00:11:08.918
The other two places are things that

00:11:08.918 --> 00:11:11.297
you can't really get anywhere else.

00:11:11.297 --> 00:11:13.641
My Worth It winner was
the pour over coffee

00:11:13.641 --> 00:11:15.355
from Coffee Elementary School.

00:11:15.355 --> 00:11:18.490
It might be my favorite
Worth It location ever.

00:11:18.490 --> 00:11:21.149
- The Münch. That place,
it's like when you shake

00:11:21.149 --> 00:11:24.049
the president's hand.
The feeling of that shake

00:11:24.049 --> 00:11:27.012
will resonate with you
for the next 24 hours.

00:11:27.012 --> 00:11:29.984
But I gotta say R.O.Star is where it's at.

00:11:29.984 --> 00:11:31.621
I'm changing my name to Starvin Lin.

00:11:31.621 --> 00:11:32.887
Rie, who's your Worth It winner?

00:11:32.887 --> 00:11:36.654
- My Worth It winner is
Coffee Elementary School.

00:11:36.654 --> 00:11:38.367
It was a great cup of coffee.

00:11:38.367 --> 00:11:41.284
- Adam, who's your Worth It Winner?

00:11:42.388 --> 00:11:46.163
I knew all you fancy
kids were gonna say that.

00:11:46.163 --> 00:11:48.629
That's okay, 'cause R.O.Star,

00:11:48.629 --> 00:11:49.994
you're always going to warm my heart,

00:11:49.994 --> 00:11:52.553
'cause you're 100 yen. Okay,
that does it for part two

00:11:52.553 --> 00:11:56.674
of three for Japan. Stay tuned
for the next episode which

00:11:56.674 --> 00:12:01.052
comes out next week where we
take on Rie's favorite thing.

00:12:01.052 --> 00:12:02.385
- Cakes. Right?

